# README Documentation Guidelines

> file_patterns: ["README.md", "**/README.md"]
> description: Standards for writing and maintaining README documentation

## Core Principles

### Deep Code Analysis
- Must understand core code implementation first
- Extract key technical features and innovations
- Avoid generic content

### Practical Orientation
- Design navigation from problem perspective
- Point to key functions and features
- Provide complete code examples

### Emphasis
- Core functionality first
- Configuration information centralized
- Performance metrics clearly listed

## Quick Navigation

### Key File Index
- File name with one-line core functionality description
- Function-based search (specific problems to specific solutions)
- Clear directory structure
- Reference to directory-specific READMEs (README_*.md)

### System Design
- Core features (with code examples)
- Key configurations (environment variables, recommended parameters)
- Architecture explanation (component relationships, data flow)
- Directory organization and relationships

## Directory Documentation
> required: true

### Directory-Specific READMEs
- Each major directory must have a README_<DIR>.md
- Follow directory-specific README guidelines
- Link to relevant subdirectory documentation
- Maintain consistency across documentation

### Directory Structure
- Document overall project structure
- Explain directory organization
- Reference directory-specific guidelines
- Maintain directory relationship diagram

## Core Functionality

### Usage Examples
- Must be directly runnable code
- Include key parameter explanations
- Show typical usage scenarios
- Link to directory-specific examples

### Configuration Details
- Complete environment variable listing
- Parameter recommendation explanations
- Performance benchmark baselines
- Directory-specific configurations

### Important Notes
- Error handling recommendations
- Performance optimization guide
- Development suggestions
- Directory-specific considerations

## Format Standards

### Markdown Usage
- Use standard Markdown syntax
- Specify language for code blocks
- Clear hierarchical structure
- Consistent formatting across all READMEs

### Content Organization
- Group related information
- Use consistent formatting
- Keep sections focused
- Follow directory-specific patterns

### Maintenance
- Regular updates with changes
- Version compatibility notes
- Migration guides when needed
- Synchronize with directory READMEs

## Validation Requirements
- README must be clear and comprehensive
- Code examples must be tested and working
- Structure must be logical and navigable
- Content must be up to date
- All required directory READMEs must exist
- Directory documentation must be consistent 